BOUNDARY: The empty space, a singleton space, and finite spaces with two or more points were each checked.  In the empty and singleton cases the Hausdorff (and therefore \(T_{1}\)) condition holds vacuously; the argument that every subset is finite and therefore closed remains valid, giving the discrete topology.  The product-step also holds because the product of discrete spaces is discrete for any finite index set.  No counterexample exists.

